      <div type="clause" n="6.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Rect">Rect</ref> 6.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="449" ed="#liebermann"/>[6.1] On manegu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> landu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> stent, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he sylle ælce geare XV swyn to sticunge, X ealde ⁊ V gynge — hæbbe sylf, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he ofer þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> arære —; on manegu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> landu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> gebyreð deopre swanriht.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="6.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="449" ed="#liebermann"/>[6.1] In multis locis stat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Rect_6-1.lnote.oe.1"/>, ut det singulis annis XV porcos ad occisionem, X ueteres et V iuuenes — ipse autem habeat superaugmentum —; in multis locis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Rect_6-1.lnote.oe.2"/> est<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Rect_6-1.lnote.oe.3"/> seruilius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Rect_6-1.lnote.oe.4"/> rectum porcarii<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Rect_6-1.lnote.oe.5"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#gobbitt" n="7.1" corresp="#wit-b">On manegum landum stent þæt he sylle ælce geare . xv . swyn to sticunge . x. ealde . 7.v. gynge . hæb|be sylf þæt he ofer þæt arære .</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="324" ed="#rabin-doml"/>On manegum landum stent þæt he sylle ælce geare XV swyn to sticunge, X ealde and V gynge, hæbbe sylf þæt he ofer þæt arære. On manegum landum gebyreð deopre swanriht.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="449" ed="#liebermann"/>Auf vielen Landgütern gilt, dass er in jedem Jahre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#Rect_6-1.lnote.de1.b"/> 15 Schweine zum Abstechen liefere, 10 ausgewachsene<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Rect_6-1.lnote.de.1"/> und 5 junge — behalte er selbst, was er darüber aufzüchtet —; auf vielen Landgütern steht schwerere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Rect_6-1.lnote.de.2"/> Schweinehirtenpflicht fest.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">On many estates it holds that he deliver [to the lord] each year 15 pigs for slaughter, 10 full-grown and 5 young — let him keep himself what he rears beyond that —; on many estates a heavier swineherd's duty is laid down.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#gobbitt" corresp="#wit-b">On many estates [the custom] stands that he gives each year fifteen pigs for slaughter, ten mature and five young. He has [for] himself [any] that he rears over that [amount].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="325" ed="#rabin-doml"/>On many estates, it is the practice that every year he gives fifteen swine for slaughter, ten mature and five young, and that he keep for himself whatever he should raise over that. On many estates, greater obligations are expected from the swineherd.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rect_6-1.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">449</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">est <hi rend="italic">MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">est MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rect_6-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">449</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr. R; fehlt MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above R; missing in MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rect_6-1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">449</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">s. r. est <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">s. r. est T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rect_6-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">449</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">seruul. <hi rend="italic">unterpunctirt, dahinter</hi> seruulus <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">seruul. underdotted, followed by seruulus R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rect_6-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">449</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ari <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ari T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Rect_6-1.lnote.de1.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">449</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">der Herrschaft</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">to the lordship</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Rect_6-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">250</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht ‘alte’ (Leo); <hi rend="italic">s. u</hi>. 13{h}</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not ‘old’ (Leo); <hi rend="italic">see below</hi> 13{h}</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Rect_6-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">250</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht ‘geringer’ (Leo). <hi rend="italic">Vgl. ius porcorum, quos porcarii debent habere</hi>; Urk. c. a. 905 Bi 618</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not ‘lesser’ (Leo). <hi rend="italic">Cf. ius porcorum, quos porcarii debent habere</hi>; charter c. a. 905 Bi 618</seg></note>
      </div>
